module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Projective
public import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.FreeModule.Basic
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.LocalRing.MaximalIdeal.Basic

/-!
# A projective-module element lies in a free direct summand

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tag 0592, lemma-projective-freeness-criteria
(blueprint: lem-trf-projective-element-free-summand).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v

open Submodule

namespace Module

/--
Let `R` be a commutative local ring and `P` a projective `R`-module. Every element
of `P` belongs to a free direct summand of `P`. The direct-sum clause is `IsCompl G H`,
which says that `G` and `H` have zero intersection and span `P`, equivalently that
every element has a unique sum from the two submodules. No finite-generation
hypothesis is imposed on `P` or `G`.

The source is Stacks Project, Algebra, Tag 0592, lemma-projective-freeness-criteria
(blueprint: lem-trf-projective-element-free-summand). The proof follows the seven
split steps recorded in the node. (1) The direct-summand characterization of
projectivity embeds `P` in a free module and gives its complementary kernel; the
zero element uses the zero free summand. (2) A basis of the ambient free module is
chosen with minimal finite support for `x`; an elementary basis shear removes any
coefficient generated by the others. (3) Applying the retraction to the support
basis gives coefficient equations for the resulting vectors. (4) The local
unit criterion makes the diagonal coefficients units and the off-diagonal ones
nonunits. (5) The Leibniz determinant formula puts the determinant in the unit
class, and the adjugate identities give an inverse matrix. (6) The resulting
finite block basis change has an explicit inverse, so the changed vectors and the
remaining basis vectors form a basis. (7) Their span is a finite free submodule
`G`; intersecting the old complementary span with `P` gives `H`, and the
coefficient expression puts `x` in `G`.
-/
theorem projective_element_mem_free_summand {R : Type u} {P : Type v} [CommRing R]
    [AddCommGroup P] [Module R P] [IsLocalRing R] [Module.Projective R P] (x : P) :
    ∃ (G H : Submodule R P), IsCompl G H ∧ x ∈ G ∧ Module.Free R G := by
  sorry

end Module

end
